+++ b/docs/WEB_SECURITY_MODEL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+# JeRyu Web Security Model
+
+Non-negotiable invariants:
+
+1. All writes require RBAC.
+2. High/critical writes require action preview and audit.
+3. Merge approvals are bound to exact head SHA.
+4. Markdown HTML is sanitized server-side.
+5. WebSocket topics enforce authorization.
+6. Secrets values never leave the backend.
+7. API tokens are hashed at rest.
+8. Cookie-auth mutating requests require CSRF.
+9. Dangerous actions require idempotency keys.
+10. Audit records are append-only and include actor/resource/risk/request ID.
+
+Permission keys are documented in the engineering spec and implemented by `src/web/rbac.rs`.
